{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SPyChx8Z5uTDwdGrDvP2WH","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is the full content of the requirements you requested from the srd053-sort.yaml file:\n\n**R4.1 (Context):**\n```\nMust exit 0 when input is sorted successfully.\n```\n\n**R4.2:**\n```\n-c or --check must check whether input is sorted. Exit 0 if sorted, exit 1 if not. With -C or --check=quiet, suppress the diagnostic message.\n```\n\n**R4.3:**\n```\nMust exit 2 on usage errors (invalid flags, conflicting options).\n```\n\n**R4.4:**\n```\nDifferential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils. Tests must cover: default sort, -r, -n, -h, -M, -V, -u, -s, -k with field specs, -t delimiter, -b, -c check mode, multi-file input, and stdin.\n```\n\nThese requirements are part of the R4 section titled \"Exit codes and differential testing\". R4.1 establishes the baseline exit code behavior (0 on success), R4.2 adds the check mode functionality with quiet option support, R4.3 specifies error handling with exit code 2, and R4.4 defines the comprehensive differential testing requirements comparing the Go implementation against the GNU sort reference binary."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b139998-cefb-41d3-bcee-99a798f067f0","uuid":"f1eee158-dc50-4027-827d-1aa6998ea8c6","timestamp":"2026-05-20T22:37:41.792Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Read the file docs/specs/software-requirements/srd053-sort.yaml in the repository at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5379. I need to see the full content, especially requirements R4.2, R4.3, and R4.4. Also look at R4.1 for context on what's already implemented. Report back the full text of these requirements.","agentId":"a66ed29dfe46475b1","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is the full content of the requiremen