{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via an automated cobbler orchestrator) has assigned task #5379: implement three remaining requirements for `cmd/sort` from srd053-sort.yaml:\n   - **R4.2**: Add `-c`/`--check` mode that checks whether input is sorted (exit 0 if sorted, exit 1 if not), and `-C`/`--check=quiet` to suppress diagnostic messages.\n   - **R4.3**: Exit code 2 on usage errors (invalid flags, conflicting options).\n   - **R4.4**: Comprehensive differential tests comparing the Go sort binary against `gsort` reference binary via `pkg/testutils`. Tests must cover: default sort, -r, -n, -h, -M, -V, -u, -s, -k with field specs, -t delimiter, -b, -c check mode, multi-file input, and stdin.\n   \n   Requirements R1.1 through R4.1 are already implemented. The task is to extend the existing implementation and add/extend tests.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: compare Go binary output against GNU reference binary (`gsort`)\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` and `pkg/testutils.BuildBinary` for test harness\n   - `DiffTest` struct: `{ Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles }`\n   - All tests must set `LC_ALL=C` in the `Env` field\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"gsort\")` with `t.Skip` if not found\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Copyright header required: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` / `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max\n   - File size limit: 500 lines max\n   - No git commands allowed (managed externally by orchestrator)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **cmd/sort/main.go** (exists, to be modified)\n     - Contains existing R1.1-R4.1 implementation (basic sort with flag