 Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}},\n91\t\t\t{Name: \"e-hex-lower\", Args: []string{\"-e\", `\\x6f`}, Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}},\n92\t\t\t{Name: \"e-hex-no-digits\", Args: []string{\"-e\", `\\xZZ`}, Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}},\n93\t\t\t// R2.1: unknown escape passes through literally\n94\t\t\t{Name: \"e-unknown-escape\", Args: []string{\"-e\", `\\q`}, Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}},\n95\t\t\t// R2.1: multiple escapes in one string\n96\t\t\t{Name: \"e-multiple-escapes\", Args: []string{\"-e\", `\\t\\n\\a`}, Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}},\n97\t\t\t// R2.2: \\c suppresses further arguments too\n98\t\t\t{Name: \"e-c-multi-arg\", Args: []string{\"-e\", `before\\c`, \"after\"}, Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}},\n99\t\t\t// R2.2: \\c at start\n100\t\t\t{Name: \"e-c-at-start\", Args: []string{\"-e\", `\\crest`}, Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}},\n101\t\t\t// R2.3: -E with backslash sequences written literally\n102\t\t\t{Name: \"E-literal-backslash-n\", Args: []string{\"-E\", `a\\nb`}, Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}},\n103\t\t\t// R2.4: -eE combined in single flag (last char wins)\n104\t\t\t{Name: \"eE-combined-flag\", Args: []string{\"-eE\", `a\\tb`}, Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}},\n105\t\t\t// R2.4: -Ee combined in single flag (last char wins)\n106\t\t\t{Name: \"Ee-combined-flag\", Args: []string{\"-Ee\", `a\\tb`}, Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}},\n107\t\t\t// R2.4: multiple separate flags, last wins\n108\t\t\t{Name: \"e-E-e-last-wins\", Args: []string{\"-e\", \"-E\", \"-e\", `a\\tb`}, Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}},\n109\t\t\t// combined -n with -E then -e\n110\t\t\t{Name: \"n-E-e-combined\", Args: []string{\"-n\", \"-E\", \"-e\", `a\\tb`}, Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}},\n111\t\t}\n112\t\ttestutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n113\t}\n114\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyz